hypotheses.statement:
Suppose $P=P^*=P^2\in\operatorname{M}_m(\mathbb Q[G])$, an odd $D>0$ clears its denominators, and $\bar P=uv$ factors through $r\ge1$ columns. Let $q=2^k>1$ satisfy $q\equiv1\pmod D$. Choose arbitrary integral lifts $U,V$ of the factors supplied by Lemma <a href="#lem:lift" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:lift">5</a>. Then $$\label{eq:integral-matrix}
 A=\begin{pmatrix}
 qI_r&V\\
 U&q^{-1}\bigl(UV-P-q(I_m-P)\bigr)
 \end{pmatrix}
 \in\operatorname{M}_{r+m}(\mathbb Z[G])$$ has an inverse in $\operatorname{M}_{r+m}(\mathbb Q[G])$.

Let $G$ be a discrete group, $m,r\ge1$, and let $P=P^*=P^2\in\operatorname{M}_m(\mathbb Q[G])$. Suppose an odd $D>0$ clears its denominators and $\bar P=uv$ with $u\in\operatorname{M}_{m,r}(\mathbb F_2[G])$ and $v\in\operatorname{M}_{r,m}(\mathbb F_2[G])$. For every $q=2^k>1$ congruent to one modulo $D$, the matrix $A$ of Lemma <a href="#lem:integral" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:integral">6</a> satisfies $$\begin{aligned}
 \tau_{r+m}(\log(T_A^*T_A))
   &=2(r-\tau_m(P))\log q,\label{eq:criterion-trace}\\
 \log\det_{\mathcal N(G)}(T_A)&=(r-\tau_m(P))\log q.
 \label{eq:criterion-det}
\end{aligned}$$ It is integral and rationally invertible, and its positive-square spectral measure has support in a compact subinterval of $(0,\infty)$.

